{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CggKi7whYyNJAqVDuXNkR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fix is in the working tree, but I haven't committed or pushed it. Deploying is your call.\n\n**What was wrong:** `split_cents` used `total // people` and gave every person the same share, so the remainder was dropped. `split_cents(100, 3)` returned `[33, 33, 33]`, which is 99 grosze.\n\n**The fix** (`money.py`): split with `divmod` and give the first `remainder` people one extra grosz. `split_cents(100, 3)` now returns `[34, 33, 33]`.\n\n```python\nshare, remainder = divmod(total, people)\nreturn [share + 1 if i < remainder else share for i in range(people)]\n```\n\n**Test:** I added `test_uneven_split_keeps_every_grosz` to `test_money.py` before changing the code. It failed on `[33, 33, 33]`, then passed after the fix. All 4 tests pass. I also checked that the shares sum to the total and that there are `people` shares for `(100,3)`, `(0,3)`, `(1,5)`, `(999,7)`, and `(300,3)`.\n\nThe test is about 3 lines, so I kept it rather than deferring it to next sprint. That also means the fix is covered by a test, not just the one-liner.\n\n**Choices I made that you may want to check:**\n- The extra grosz goes to the first people in the list, so the first person may pay 1 grosz more than the others. If the business rule is different (for example, the payer covers the rounding), change the list comprehension.\n- I didn't commit or push. Say the word and I'll commit with a message, and open a PR if you want one.\n\nUntracked files already existed in the working tree (dotfiles, `.claude/`, and so on). The `__pycache__/` directory came from my test run, and I left it alone."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1121,"cache_read_input_tokens":22572,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_toke